  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through multiple pathways, ultimately targeting Detroit 98 via distinct molecular mechanisms. The first pathway links Oblonganoside C to Caov-4, which is targeted by K-252a, a small molecule that itself targets Detroit 98. The second pathway connects Oblonganoside C to Serine/threonine-protein kinase SBK1, which is targeted by Theasaponin E1, another compound that also targets Detroit 98. The third pathway reveals that Oblonganoside C targets Tyrosine-protein kinase Fes/Fps, which is targeted by a complex compound with a long chain hydroxy group structure, also leading to Detroit 98. These diverse targets suggest that Oblonganoside C may act through different signaling pathways to influence the activity of Detroit 98, potentially through the modulation of kinase activity or other cellular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, with Detroit 98 being a downstream effector in multiple signaling cascades initiated by Oblonganoside C.",
